# App Shell Sidebar Animation Pattern

Use this pattern for **every** collapsible sidebar panel in the app — secondary nav, chat session sidebar, agents workspace sidebar, or any future custom sidebar.

## Two-sidebar pattern (inline + overlay)

Every collapsible sidebar requires **two** elements rendered in parallel:

1. **Inline panel** — always mounted, takes layout space, animates its width between `0` and its natural width.
2. **Hover overlay panel** — absolutely positioned, slides in via `translateX`, shown on hover over the toggle button. Only rendered when the sidebar is closed.

### Inline panel

```tsx
<div
  className={cn(
    "hidden shrink-0 overflow-hidden transition-[width] duration-300 ease-in-out md:flex",
    isOpen ? "w-72" : "w-0"   // use the sidebar's natural width
  )}
>
  {/* min-w must match the natural width to prevent content reflowing */}
  <div className="flex min-h-0 min-w-72 flex-1 flex-col">{sidebar}</div>
</div>
```

- Use `transition-[width] duration-300 ease-in-out` — never `hidden`/`block` toggling.
- The inner wrapper's `min-w-*` must equal the sidebar's natural width so content doesn't reflow while animating.
- Add `shell-divider` on the outer column when you need the shared shell theme hook (borders are transparent in `theme-lines` / `theme-floating` / `theme-paper` so the column does not draw a line against main content). At `w-0`, avoid stacking extra borders on the inline strip.

```tsx
className={cn(
  "hidden shrink-0 overflow-hidden transition-[width] duration-300 ease-in-out md:flex",
  isOpen ? "shell-divider w-72" : "w-0"
)}
```

### Hover overlay panel

```tsx
{!isOpen ? (
  <div
    className={cn(
      "absolute inset-y-0 left-0 z-30 hidden w-72 flex-col overflow-hidden md:flex",
      "border-border border-r bg-card/98 shadow-xl backdrop-blur-sm",
      "transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out",
      hoverOpen
        ? "translate-x-0"
        : "pointer-events-none -translate-x-full"
    )}
    onMouseEnter={openHoverPanel}
    onMouseLeave={closeHoverPanel}
  >
    {sidebar}
  </div>
) : null}
```

- Parent container must have `relative` positioning.
- Parent must have `overflow-hidden` — this clips the panel while it is translated off-screen (left of the container boundary), which makes it slide in from the edge correctly.
- Use `pointer-events-none -translate-x-full` when hidden so the invisible panel never intercepts clicks on the main content.

### Hover state with debounce

Use a 150 ms close-debounce so the panel stays open when the mouse moves between the toggle button (in the topbar) and the panel below it:

```tsx
const [hoverOpen, setHoverOpen] = useState(false);
const hoverTimeoutRef = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null>(null);

const openHoverPanel = useCallback(() => {
  if (hoverTimeoutRef.current) {
    clearTimeout(hoverTimeoutRef.current);
    hoverTimeoutRef.current = null;
  }
  setHoverOpen(true);
}, []);

const closeHoverPanel = useCallback(() => {
  hoverTimeoutRef.current = setTimeout(() => setHoverOpen(false), 150);
}, []);

// Clear hover when pinned open or nav items disappear
useEffect(() => {
  if (isOpen || !hasSidebar) setHoverOpen(false);
}, [isOpen, hasSidebar]);

// Cleanup on unmount
useEffect(() => {
  return () => {
    if (hoverTimeoutRef.current) clearTimeout(hoverTimeoutRef.current);
  };
}, []);
```

## Toggle button wiring

### Secondary nav (AppLayout → AppTopbar)

Pass hover callbacks via `AppTopbar` props. They are only active when the nav is closed:

```tsx
// AppTopbar.tsx — secondary nav button
<Button
  onMouseEnter={!secondaryNavOpen ? onSecondaryNavHoverEnter : undefined}
  onMouseLeave={!secondaryNavOpen ? onSecondaryNavHoverLeave : undefined}
  onClick={onToggleSecondaryNav}
  ...
/>
```

Pass from `AppLayoutFrame`:
```tsx
<AppTopbar
  onSecondaryNavHoverEnter={openHoverPanel}
  onSecondaryNavHoverLeave={closeHoverPanel}
  ...
/>
```

### agentsWorkspaceNav sidebars (chat, agents workspace)

Add `onHoverEnter` / `onHoverLeave` to the `AgentsWorkspaceNavRegistration` (defined in `packages/ui-plugin-sdk/src/page-config.tsx`). `AppTopbar` wires them to the `agentsWorkspaceNav` button automatically when closed:

```tsx
// AppTopbar.tsx — agentsWorkspaceNav button
<Button
  onMouseEnter={!agentsWorkspaceNav.open ? agentsWorkspaceNav.onHoverEnter : undefined}
  onMouseLeave={!agentsWorkspaceNav.open ? agentsWorkspaceNav.onHoverLeave : undefined}
  ...
/>
```

Register in the page component:
```tsx
useAgentsWorkspaceNavRegistration({
  open: sidebarOpen,
  setOpen: setSidebarOpen,
  onHoverEnter: openHoverPanel,   // optional but required for hover preview
  onHoverLeave: closeHoverPanel,
  toggleAriaLabelWhenClosed: "...",
  toggleAriaLabelWhenOpen: "...",
});
```

## Checklist for new sidebars

- [ ] Outer container has `relative` + `overflow-hidden`
- [ ] Inline panel uses `transition-[width] duration-300 ease-in-out` (not conditional render)
- [ ] Inner wrapper has `min-w-*` equal to sidebar's natural width
- [ ] `shell-divider` applied only when open (not at `w-0`)
- [ ] Hover overlay uses `translate-x` with `pointer-events-none` when hidden
- [ ] Hover state uses 150 ms debounce on close
- [ ] Toggle button in topbar passes hover callbacks (do NOT put trigger strip on content edge)
- [ ] Hover state cleared when sidebar is pinned open
- [ ] Timeout cleaned up on unmount
